Job description :

Do you have a strong background in IT product management and industrial applications within an aerospace manufacturing environment, and would you like to progress and develop new skills? Then this job is for you!
The A220 commercial aircraft Programme is looking for an Industrial Solutions Product Manager to join our Airbus Digital North America team in Mirabel (Québec, Canada),
The team organization is established to promote cross-collaboration autonomously, supporting each other and learning collectively.

The Industrial Solutions A220 Product Manager is responsible for all functional and technical IM-related activities of Industrial Shopfloor Solutions Product & Services specifically dedicated to the Airbus A220 program (including Mirabel FAL & Plant and Mobile FAL).
The role ensures strategic alignment of the IM roadmap with the A220 ramp-up and production milestones, deploying Airbus standards on Data Lineage, Data Consumption, and Smart Execution. The incumbent will promote a multi-site approach, integrating local A220 shopfloor constraints into the Group's governance and transnational Operating Model.
Serves as a senior strategic leader responsible for steering mid- to long-term digital strategy while managing and maintaining a complex, multi-site industrial setup across transnational manufacturing teams.

Your working environment:

The A220 commercial aircraft Programme is headquartered in Mirabel, in the greater Montreal area, where the vibrant city of Montreal is just a stone’s throw away. Known for its peaceful and safe environment, the region offers a high quality of life for younger or experienced professionals and families, perfectly balancing career opportunities and outdoor activities that makes it a truly special place to call home.

How we care for you:

- Financial rewards: Attractive salary, annual bonus, group insurance plan, pension plan and share purchase plan.
- Work / Life Balance: A hybrid working policy (based on operational needs), on-site cafeterias and a highly competitive holiday policy.
- Wellbeing/Health: Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Discount Program, on-site Medical Service, access to a public shuttle service between Laval (Montmorency metro station) and Mirabel, and a carpooling application.
- Individual development: Great upskilling opportunities and development prospects with unlimited access to +10.000 e-learning courses to develop your employability, certifications, accelerated development programmes, national and international mobility.

Your challenges:

- Assume end-to-end functional and technical responsibility for the performance (delivery, costs, team management, and well-being) of the A220 Industrial Shopfloor Solutions product scope across its full lifecycle (Design / Build / Run);
- Form and lead Multi-Functional Teams (MFT) to manage the application lifecycle related to A220 Industrial Shopfloor Solutions Product & Services;
- Lead the A220 Industrial Shopfloor Solutions design authority (architecture choices and technical standards) in close collaboration with IM Enterprise Architects;
- Manage IT projects within the A220 Industrial Shopfloor Solutions scope using appropriate methodologies (Waterfall, Fast Track, Agile);
- Design, deploy, and support local applications fulfilling specific A220 business needs while deploying central Industry applications from European mother companies;
- Drive product optimization across all dimensions: financial efficiency, user experience, cyber security, resilience, and technical debt reduction;
- Manage allocation of business continuity and run budget envelopes alongside a multi-million dollar annual project budget dedicated to A220 industrial solutions evolution;
- Responsible for transnational deployment of Group IM-supported processes, information systems, and core manufacturing solutions across A220 production lines.

Your boarding pass:

- Master's Degree in Manufacturing, Engineering, Computer Science, Information Technology, or an equivalent combination of education and experience;
- At least ten (10) years of experience in application development and support in a manufacturing/shopfloor environment;
- At least five (5) – ten (10) years of Project Management experience in a manufacturing environment and large-scale Industrial Solutions deployment projects;
- Domain Expertise: Strong knowledge of shopfloor operations, Final Assembly Lines (FAL), manufacturing engineering, quality, and aerospace logistics;
- Technical Systems Proficiency: IIoT, SCADA, industrial machine connectivity, MES, PLC integrations, SAP (PM, SAP S4/HANA), and Analytics Solutions;
- Soft Skills: Proven ability to lead multicultural and multi-site teams, adapt to a rapidly changing ramp-up environment, and interact effectively with senior business stakeholders;
- Fluency in English is mandatory. Fluency in French is highly recommended, and knowledge of German or Spanish is a plus.

This role may involve travel (approx. 10% Domestic and International - US, EU limited).

Due to the sector of activity (aerospace), frequent contacts with Airbus entities worldwide, and interactions with suppliers and clients also located across the globe, proficiency in English is required for this position.

